"'''All of Me'''" is a song by American singer [[John Legend]] from his fourth [[studio album]] ''[[Love in the Future]]'' (2013). It is dedicated to Legend's wife [[Chrissy Teigen]].     "All of Me" first aired on American [[urban contemporary|mainstream urban]] radio as the album's third single on August 12, 2013.

On the week ending May 17, 2014, it peaked at number one on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], becoming his first number-one single in the United States. It knocked off "[[Happy (Pharrell Williams song)|Happy]]" by [[Pharrell Williams]], which had spent 10 weeks at number one. The song peaked at number two in the United Kingdom, South Africa and [[New Zealand]] and topped the charts in Australia, Canada, Ireland, Portugal, Sweden, Switzerland and the [[Netherlands]]. It became the second best-selling song of 2014 in the United States with 4.67 million copies sold for the year,<ref name="us sales 2014">{{cite web |url=https://www.yahoo.com/music/its-official-pharrell-has-2014s-best-selling-106748836876.html |title=It's Official: Pharrell Has 2014's Best-Selling Song |first =Paul|last =Grein |date=December 31, 2014 |work=Yahoo! Music }}</ref> as well as the third best-selling song in the United Kingdom.<ref name="Top 40 2014">{{cite web|first= Rob |last= Copsey |url= http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/the-official-top-40-biggest-selling-singles-of-2014-3389/ |title= The UK's most downloaded song ever revealed! |publisher= [[Official Charts Company]] |date= January 1, 2014 |access-date= January 1, 2015}}</ref> "All of Me" was the third best-selling song of 2014 with 12.3 million equivalent-units worldwide (sales plus streaming), according to the IFPI.<ref name="Ifpi2015">{{cite web |title= IFPI publishes Digital Music Report 2015 |url= http://www.ifpi.org/news/Global-digital-music-revenues-match-physical-format-sales-for-first-time |publisher= International Federation of the Phonographic Industry |date= April 14, 2015 |access-date= April 15, 2015 |page= 12 |archive-date= April 14, 2015 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20150414194629/http://www.ifpi.org/news/Global-digital-music-revenues-match-physical-format-sales-for-first-time |url-status= dead }}</ref>

A remix of the song (Tiësto's Birthday Treatment remix), featuring [[Electronic dance music|EDM]] artist [[Tiësto]], was released in January 2014 and won the 2015 [[Grammy Award for Best Remixed Recording, Non-Classical]], while another remix was done in March of that year by trance artist Dash Berlin. A live version of the song was nominated for [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Solo Performance|Best Pop Solo Performance]], losing to Williams' "Happy".<ref name="billboard">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/john-legend-delves-into-all-of-me-video-interview-photo-shoot-behind-the-scenes-5922947/|title=John Legend Delves Into 'All of Me': Video Q&A + Photo Shoot Behind-The-Scenes|magazine=Billboard |access-date=April 6, 2014}}</ref>

